        "default": null,
        "description": "Per-source filters. Each source accepts only its own keys:\n  messages (and email, gmail, imessage, whatsapp): person, since, path\n  network: path\n  shared_project_agents: project_id, path (safe metadata only)\n  agent_network: path, role\n  agent_trajectories: path, since, until, role, surface, record_kind\n  transactions: since, until, account, min_amount, max_amount, status ('posted', 'pending', or 'all'), include_pending_in_totals, path\n  documents: document_source, since, until, tag, path\n  calendar, drive: since, until, path\nA flat key ({\"since\": \"7d\"}) applies to every selected source that accepts it. To target one source, nest its keys under the source name: {\"calendar\": {\"since\": \"2026-11-02\"}}; a messages block covers email, gmail, imessage and whatsapp. documents is an umbrella corpus, so set document_source to the concrete provider (chatgpt, claude, apple_notes, obsidian, or granola). granola covers every Granola meeting; granola_note (title, time, attendees, own notes), granola_summary or granola_transcript searches just that layer. `path` takes a path from an earlier result (e.g. 'network/Andy Prevalsky.contact', 'messages/+15551234567.thread') to scope that path's own source to the record or thread; for agent_network and agent_trajectories it may instead be an agent address such as /root/outreach. A calendar or drive path may also be a folder of a result path, such as 'calendar/<account>/2026-10-02' or 'drive/<account>/My Drive/Legal'. Calendar since and until take a date (YYYY-MM-DD) and include that whole day; with neither, calendar lists from yesterday onward."
